  "Question": "The value of \\((256)^{0.16}\\cdot(256)^{0.09}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(16\\)",
    "C": "\\(64\\)",
    "D": "\\(256.25\\)",
    "E": "\\(-16\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The factors have the same positive base, so multiplying them adds their exponents:\n\\[\n256^{0.16}\\cdot256^{0.09}\n=256^{0.16+0.09}\n=256^{0.25}\n=256^{1/4}.\n\\]\nThe exponent \\(1/4\\) means the positive fourth root. Since \\(4^4=256\\), the value is \\(4\\), choice A.",
